  "about": "Common English names for well-known Bible passages, mapped to references. Used by the controller's typed input (fallback when a reference does not parse) and by voice (final segments with no detected reference). English aliases are first-class. Tamil coverage is intentionally sparse and community-growable.",
  "contributing": "To add an alias: append an object to entries with a canonical name, an aliases array of alternate English phrasings (lowercase, no punctuation needed), and ref as either a single reference string or an array of 2-3 strings where accounts differ. Every ref MUST be within a single chapter (the parser does not span chapters); pick a representative chapter/verse-range for multi-chapter narratives. For Tamil, add a ta array ONLY with phrasing you can source from the bundled Tamil translation's own book/passage vocabulary or a confident transliteration of a proper name; do not invent Tamil phrasing you are unsure of. A unit test verifies every ref parses.",
  "license": "The alias curation is MIT with the rest of the project. Reference targets are not copyrighted.",
